[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   step_19: N-body planetary baseline -- REBOUND integration of the CODE comets.
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   step_040 built the planetary baseline from an analytic Jupiter
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   encounter proxy.  This step replaces the proxy with a genuine
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   symplectic-family N-body integration:
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   For each class-1 CODE comet the osculating elements at the
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   perihelion epoch T (TT) are converted to a heliocentric state
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   vector and integrated BACKWARD through the full planetary system
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   (Sun + planetary-system barycentres 1-9, states from JPL DE440s
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   rotated ICRF-equatorial -> ecliptic J2000) with REBOUND/IAS15.
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   The integration stops when the comet reaches 255 AU, matching
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   the 250 AU asymptote at which the catalogue's original orbit is
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   defined.  A MERCURIUS (hybrid-symplectic, close-encounter
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   switching) re-integration of the full sample provides an
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   integrator-independence check.
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   Kick metrics per comet:
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   kick_e  = 1/a_osc - 1/a_out   [10^-6 AU^-1]  (energy kick;
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   sign convention matches catalogue delta(1/a))
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   denc    = minimum comet-planet distance over the integration
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   [AU] and the dominant perturber
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   Validation: the catalogue's own original-vs-osculating energy
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   change cat_kick = 1/a_osc - 1/a_orig is an independent N-body
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   measurement of the same planetary perturbation.  The simulated
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   and catalogue kicks are compared statistically across the
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   sample (deep-encounter comets are chaos-limited, so the
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   comparison is reported both full-sample and trimmed).
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   Baseline regression mirrors step_040:
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   log(d_of) ~ 1 + |kick_e| + q  -> residuals -> cap contrast
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   (Mann-Whitney, greater) and continuous Spearman test.
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   Outputs
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   results/step_19_nbody_planetary_baseline.json
[2026-09-20 12:08:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 042]   results/step_19_nbody_kicks.csv   (per-comet kick table)
